      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Palisades Interstate Park’s 1930s heyday is captured in a New Deal film, complete with historic footage and park documents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://njpalisades.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Lee Historic Park sits atop the cliffs, offering a reconstructed Revolutionary War encampment and a visitor center that tells the area’s wartime story.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://njpalisades.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Hudson River below the Palisades has witnessed countless historic moments, from early ferry crossings to modern military defenses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://njpalisades.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first concerted effort to preserve the Palisades began in the 1890s, led by the American Scenic and Historic Preservation Society.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://njpalisades.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "On the clifftops, historic sites range from Skunk Hollow to Millionaire’s Row, showcasing the region’s diverse heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
